{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794218903,"nonce":"bo7nM7/wd1047BcfFPmKrzPnIrk=","message":"Host interop in the working tree (uncommitted). The compiler reports a Reflection with the artifacts: the module's struct layouts (offsets and sizes by WGSL's rules, checked against naga's own layout of the emitted WGSL in tests/reflect.rs), the bindings emitted with group, binding, kind and buffer size, the pipeline constants at the values the artifact was built with (read from naga after process_overrides), each vertex entry point's location inputs with their wgpu::VertexFormat, and the struct imports.\n\nrussl_expand turns it into Rust next to the artifacts: a #[repr(C)] twin per struct with explicit padding fields, so its bytes are exactly a buffer's (vectors as arrays, a Vec3 in an array as [f32; 4] for its stride, matrix columns padded the same way, f16 as u16 bits, a runtime-sized tail documented rather than held); new(..), zeroed(), as_bytes(), slice_as_bytes(), SIZE and \u003cFIELD\u003e_OFFSET; size and offset_of! asserted at build time. #![bytemuck] in a shader adds unsafe Pod and Zeroable impls through ::bytemuck. Bindings become \u003cNAME\u003e_GROUP, \u003cNAME\u003e_BINDING and \u003cNAME\u003e_SIZE, CONSTANTS is wgpu's (name, f64) list as built (a specialisation lists its own values), and \u003cENTRY\u003e_INPUTS the vertex inputs.\n\nThe open question (a struct shared by shaders in several crates): the struct lives in a russl library module, whose expansion holds its twin; every module's struct imports are mirrored as Rust use items (pub use for pub use), so a twin naming an imported struct resolves to the one twin, through re-export chains and across crates. The prelude's structs are the framework's own and are not mirrored.\n\nThe issue's typed-overrides struct no longer fits: pipeline constants are fixed when the shader is built (5976a11), so CONSTANTS reports them instead.\n\nNot covered: russl_build writing host Rust for file programs. Tests: tests/reflect.rs (2, layouts against naga), crates/russl/tests/host.rs (2, a shared struct inside a shader struct, bytes at offsets, bytemuck, binding and input consts, a variant's CONSTANTS).","files":null}]}